🇵🇭 The Philippine Navy conducted its first combat launch of the Spike NLOS missile from an AW159 helicopter

On September 9, the Philippine Navy carried out live-fire exercises using the Israeli Spike missile system in the waters west of the municipality of San Antonio in Zambales province. For the first time, an airborne launch of a Spike missile was performed from an AW159 anti-submarine helicopter. The target was successfully destroyed. Later, the missile boat "Thomas Campo" (hull number PG908) made another Spike missile launch at a different target in coordination with the helicopter.

Other assets participated in the maneuvers:

• Frigate "Miguel Malvar" (hull number FFG06);
• Boats PG909, PG907, assault boats BA492 and BA488;
• Coast guard boat "Suluan" (hull number 4406);
• UAV Scan Eagle;
• Marine Corps coastal defense units.

The exercise was part of the implementation of the "Comprehensive Archipelago Defense Concept", aimed at strengthening the maritime defense of the Philippines.

